me with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML:\n  Favours first:  autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Chronic Phase:\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues, bleeding easily\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Polycythemia Vera (PV):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia, autosomal dominant inheritance, somatic mutation\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nDe Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia vs Essential Thrombocythemia (ET):\n  Favours first:  acute myeloid leukemia\n  Favours second: abnormal cerebral vascular morphology, abnormal platelet morphology, abnormal thrombocyte morphology, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology, amaurosis fugax\n\nCML Blast Crisis (Ph+ myeloid neoplasm with blast phase) vs Myelodysplastic Syndrome with Excess Blasts / Therapy-Related AML:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal basophil morphology, abnormal granulocyte morphology, abnormal/excessive bleeding, abnormality of blood and blood-forming tissues\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal circulating albumin concentration, abnormal circulating protein concentration, abnormal mean corpuscular volume, abnormality of bone marrow cell morphology\n\nCML Blast Crisis (Ph+ myeloid neoplasm with blast phase) vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML) in Chronic Phase:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal/excessive bleeding, anemia, confusion, easy bruising\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, bleeding easily, blurred vision, enlarged spleen,